                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa42beed-d140-37ff-a664-0f5e06c0cec5",
                        "entry_id": "37d5b691-3c13-3bc0-912d-ad8c2b891d7a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An advocate for a hierarchy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eed8fc4f-d16c-4cce-ad56-bbbd7c6c20f2",
                                "sense_id": "aa42beed-d140-37ff-a664-0f5e06c0cec5",
                                "text": "The fear of corporatism, consumerism, middle-browism and a mass reading public has driven twentieth-century cultural hierarchists."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "468bfa46-4d56-4fe0-afe7-3f559dada877",
                                "sense_id": "aa42beed-d140-37ff-a664-0f5e06c0cec5",
                                "text": "Two of the groups involved, he said, are simply characterized: individualists (most people would call them libertarians, who want the government to butt out) and communitarians, the two poles on the political spectrum. The two other groups, he said, are called hierarchists and egalitarians."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
